### 3. Stage 0 for RDP audio
```bash
mkdir -p $SCRATCH/brainstorm/rdp-audio
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd $SCRATCH/brainstorm/rdp-audio --label pa-codex --no-focus
herdr agent start pa-codex --kind codex --pane <pane> --timeout 120000 -- -m gpt-6-astra -c model_reasoning_effort=xhigh -s workspace-write -a never --search
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd $SCRATCH/brainstorm/rdp-audio --label pa-fable --no-focus
herdr agent start pa-fable --kind claude --pane <pane> --timeout 120000 -- --model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh --name pa-fable
```
- Brief files `brief-rdp-audio-r1-{A,B}.txt` follow the §10a template:
  - `ROUND 1 draft — ends when your draft file is written`
  - `SKILL superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner (questions batched)`
  - `PROBLEM "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning."`
  - `FACTS` = the role paths from step 1
  - `DECIDED` = the CLAUDE.md hard rules verbatim, deploy only from merged main, canary `ccs-it` first
  - `WRITE $SCRATCH/brainstorm/rdp-audio/draft-{A,B}.md` and nothing else
  - `TIME BOX 60 min to first report`
- One background call per tab:
  `herdr agent prompt pa-codex "$(cat …r1-A.txt)" --wait --timeout 3600000; herdr agent read pa-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $SCRATCH/inbox/pa-codex.last`, and the same for `pa-fable`.
- `pa-fable` will ask for permission to write. I answer those prompts myself: yes inside its folder, no everywhere else.

### 4. Close out the relay task, in parallel
- Foreground checks and cleanup:
  - `git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive status --porcelain`: must be empty.
  - `herdr agent get wgka`: must be idle and not focused. Then `herdr tab close <wgka tab_id>`.
  - `git worktree remove …/wg-keepalive && git worktree prune && git branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay && git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible pull`.
  - `ps -p 48211 -o pid,lstart,command`: confirm it is the `codex app-server` I started at 21:30, then `kill 48211`, then `ps -p 48211` to confirm it's gone.
- Docs worktree: `git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree add .claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs -b chore/wg-keepalive-docs origin/main`.
- Agent tool, Opus, in the background. It gets the worktree's absolute path and `$SCRATCH/evidence/wg-keepalive-ccs-it.txt`. That file holds the deploy log, the `changed=0` re-run, the read-only checks and the operator's ping summary word for word. The subagent's job:
  - update `projects/ccs/soul/ccs-it.md` from that evidence only;
  - update the docs the relay affects;
  - mark the design and plan docs implemented, with PR #165.
- Then I check every claim against the evidence and run `git grep -nE "code/session_[0-9A-Za-z]"`. After that: commit, push, PR, and `gh pr merge --merge --delete-branch`, since it's docs-only. Then I remove that worktree and delete its branch.
- I write the memory note and its `MEMORY.md` line. When everything is done: backlog `done`, `docs closed: yes`, republish.

